@page "/reference/keyboard"

@* The Keyboard reference (ADR-0110), a reference page: every key of the three products, one table per
   product, each row linking the section of the page that explains it and the decision behind it. The rows
   are KeyboardByHand's, which the build checks; the selection page's own table is drawn from the same rows. *@
<DocsPage Title="Keyboard"
          Lead="Every key of ExGrid, ExSheet and ExPivot, each with the page that explains it. The keys are Excel's; Ctrl is the Command key on a Mac. ExSheet and ExPivot are drawn by ExGrid, so ExGrid's keys hold in both.">
    <ReferenceAsOf>Each row links the section that explains it, and the decision behind it.</ReferenceAsOf>

    <DocsSection Title="ExGrid">
        <KeyTable Rows="@KeyboardByHand.ExGrid" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="ExSheet">
        <KeyTable Rows="@KeyboardByHand.ExSheet" />
    </DocsSection>

    <DocsSection Title="ExPivot">
        <KeyTable Rows="@KeyboardByHand.ExPivot" />
    </DocsSection>
</DocsPage>
